From de81654d214776a030688b5b6e8485687fd97fb0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yaron Shahrabani <EMAIL>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 08:30:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] media: venus: venc: rate control from the frame rate on
 HFI 1.x

The HFI 1.x firmware (MSM8916, VIDEO.VE.1.8) budgets the bits of each
frame from the input buffer timestamps unless told otherwise. The driver
passes the V4L2 timestamps through, but those are opaque cookies to a
stateful encoder: GStreamer's v4l2 encoders, for one, set them to the
frame number in seconds. The firmware then sees one frame per second and
gives every frame the budget of a whole second. At a 2 Mbit/s VBR target
for 640x480, GStreamer got 7.4 Mbit/s on test bars and 25 Mbit/s on
noise. v4l2-ctl, which queues real timestamps faster than real time,
undershot instead. Neither S_PARM, the H.264 level nor the VUI timing
changed the result.

Send HFI_PROPERTY_PARAM_VENC_DISABLE_RC_TIMESTAMP, which the 1.x packet
builder already handles, so that the firmware uses the frame rate set
through VIDIOC_S_PARM, as the stateful encoder interface intends.

Fixes: aaaa93eda64b ("[media] media: venus: venc: add video encoder files")
Assisted-by: claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c
index 0174e6d..4a2928f 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/venus/venc.c
@@ -852,6 +852,20 @@ static int venc_set_properties(struct venus_inst *inst)
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
+	/*
+	 * Budget the bits from the frame rate (S_PARM), not from the buffer
+	 * timestamps: they are opaque cookies to the driver, and e.g.
+	 * GStreamer's v4l2 encoders use frame numbers in seconds, which made
+	 * the HFI 1.x firmware overshoot the target bitrate 4-14 times.
+	 */
+	if (IS_V1(inst->core)) {
+		ptype = HFI_PROPERTY_PARAM_VENC_DISABLE_RC_TIMESTAMP;
+		en.enable = 1;
+		ret = hfi_session_set_property(inst, ptype, &en);
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
+	}
+
 	if (rate_control == HFI_RATE_CONTROL_CQ && ctr->const_quality) {
 		struct hfi_heic_frame_quality quality = {};
 
